le value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September ran 81% of normal and November to December ran 76% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 38% of normal. Every grid had its driest year in 1987, with grid 22993 down to 62%.</p>"}
